blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1854:	Write a pair of operators, one on $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''$ and one on $\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'\mathrm{B}''$, for their simultaneous placement on the six registers.  Simultaneous placement is multiplicative, commutes with taking adjoints, sends the pair of identities to the identity, and therefore turns conjugation by a pair into conjugation on each block separately.  An arbitrary operator on one player's original register, placed on the six registers, is the placement on that player's block of the operator extended by the identity on that player's two Pauli registers, and the crossed placement of an operator on an extracted register is the placement on that block of the identity tensored with that operator.  Hence conjugating a one-sided placement by a simultaneous placement whose operators satisfy $UU^\dagger = \Id$ on each block only involves the operator of that same side.  Finally, the action of a simultaneous placement is the tensor action of the two block operators after the block reassociation of Definition~\ref{def:extraction-block-order}, it agrees with the tensor action of two linear isometries, and it preserves the norm of every vector as soon as each block operator satisfies $U^\dagger U = \Id$.  These are the placements used in the proof of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary}; no property of the swap operators of Definition~\ref{def:v-swap-unitary} is assumed here.

